course: dictionary
lesson: 11358
title: Long words with a clue inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are easier than they look. Zoological is a long word, but it is built from parts you may know. The clue here is the Zoological Society, a group that studies animals. Context tells you what the word is about: «London Zoo opened in 1828 as a zoo for science, set up by the Zoological Society of London.»
explain: Read the words around the hard word and ask: what would fit here? In «zoological research», research is about something. The clue is the word zoo, which sits inside zoological. So zoological research must be research about animals.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in "to do with animals" for zoological and read it again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Zoological is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «zoological research» or «zoological garden».
fact: «Zoological» means to do with zoology, the science of animals.
fact: «Zoological» can also mean to do with a zoo, as in «zoological garden».
fact: A zoological garden is the full old name for a zoo, and «zoo» is the short everyday word.
fact: Other phrases you may meet: zoological park, zoological society and zoological museum.
exercise: «Dr Chen does zoological research on wild birds.» What does zoological mean here? | To do with the sea and ships | *To do with the science of animals | To do with music | To do with trains and engines
exercise: The short word «zoo» comes from which longer phrase? | *zoological garden | ancient castle | zoological research | sunny seaside
exercise: «The Zoological Society of London still does research worldwide.» Find and copy the word that tells you the society is about animals. | *Zoological | worldwide | London | research
test: «The zoological park had giraffes and penguins.» What does zoological describe? | *A park to do with animals | A sad old castle | A place for swimming | A park full of trees
test: Which phrase is the full old name for a zoo? | zoological society | *zoological garden | zoological research | ancient garden
exam: In «London Zoo opened in 1828 as a zoo for science», what kind of zoo was it first? | A zoo for sport | A zoo for swimming | *A zoo for science | A zoo for shopping
